# Site content and the admin

- Brand copy, stops (the calendar), menu, hire packages, the earlier-venture story, photos, home copy, contact and social links live in `src/content/site/*.json`. FAQs are `src/content/faqs/*.md`. Never hard-code them in components, and never add env vars for them.
- `src/data/Content/schemas.ts` defines every file (`zod/mini` only: full `zod` in a shared chunk adds about 10 KB to every public page). The build loads and checks them in `site-content.ts` and fails with a plain message on a bad edit.
- Consumers read through the loaders (`Content/settings.ts`, `Stop/stops.ts`, `Content/site-content.ts` for the rest). Add a field: schema, JSON, loader; the admin form follows (see `docs/ADMIN.md`).
- Picture ids are file names in `src/assets/uploads` without extension. Photos are optional: none means the illustration leads.
- Quoted reviews on the story page are real quotes with their source. Never invent or paraphrase a review.
- The admin (`/admin/`) saves one GitHub commit. It talks only to `ContentStore` and `AdminAuth` (`features/content-admin/models`); keep it that way so protection can change without touching screens. It must stay `noindex, nofollow`, carry the CSP meta tag, load no third-party script, and stay off unless `PUBLIC_ADMIN_ENABLED=1`.
- Products are not content: they stay in Shopify.
